╔════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║  Unit 4.3: Fujisaki-Okamoto Transform                      ║
╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

=== Valid Encapsulation/Decapsulation ===

Public key (ek): 500f22ebeac67274a5f6a7ef4a9c3af0...
Rejection secret (z): e69bda8c6e6d1c72c718e9fe8974daf3...

Ciphertext: 339a68c4659f2d61081d1353219a68fb...
Sender's key: 8f244a0e9513fcf2ab2b1d04d1cee326...

Receiver's key: 8f244a0e9513fcf2ab2b1d04d1cee326...

✓ Keys MATCH - valid encapsulation

=== Invalid Ciphertext (Modified) ===

Original ciphertext: 2617e7d39016d4f0951a2538b6fe5ccf...
Sender's key: 3c26622c82e3fd9ad89887e63ea909c1...

Modified ciphertext: 2717e7d39016d4f0951a2538b6fe5ccf...
(Attacker flipped bit 0)

Receiver's key (from modified ct): ddb7d9a363067279f95dbe459f20e981...

✓ Keys DO NOT MATCH - implicit rejection triggered
  Attacker gets random-looking key, can't tell it's rejected

=== Implicit Rejection Consistency ===

Garbage ciphertext: 9417ffeb05d32d0c8ef29eb1a64c0068...
First decaps result: 85c4b52b0b4d16d3a15ebc7c475b74cd...
Second decaps result: 85c4b52b0b4d16d3a15ebc7c475b74cd...

✓ Same garbage → same key (deterministic rejection)
  This is essential: attacker can't detect rejection
  by querying same ciphertext multiple times

════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
Key Points:
  1. FO transform: CPA encryption → CCA KEM
  2. Re-encryption check detects tampering
  3. Implicit rejection: invalid → random-looking key
  4. Same invalid ct → same rejection key (consistent)
  5. All comparisons must be constant-time
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
